{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And the reason of <b>our soul is dried up</b> — that their nature grew hot from an abundance of cravings and dried up on account of it, as in the words of Onkelos (Targum Onkelos on Numbers 11:6). Or, 'our soul is dried up' because it has nothing to moisten it, for food produces moistness in the body and restores the soul to satiety. And they said, <b>nothing but this manna are our eyes</b> — that even the sustenance by which we live is not in our hands, so that our soul might grow fat and satisfied from it; rather, we crave it and lift our eyes to it at all times, for perhaps it will come to us. And so there is nothing but anticipation of the manna. They said the well-known proverb (Yoma 74a): one who has bread in his basket is not like one who has no bread in his basket. And Scripture recounted how many virtues the manna possesses, and said that its taste was like the taste of cream (leshad hashemen), to declare that the soul of those who eat it will not dry up, for it moistens and satisfies, and the soul of those who eat it shall be like a watered garden and like a spring of waters."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:18.470866511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}